Algorithm:

1. Start.
2. Input the number of elements N.
3. Generate N random numbers.
4. Display the generated random numbers.
5. Build a Max Heap from the elements.
6. Set i = N - 1.
7. Swap the first element (maximum) with a[i].
8. Reduce the heap size by 1.
9. Apply Heapify to maintain the Max Heap.
10. Repeat steps 7–9 until i = 1.
11. Display the sorted elements.
12. Stop.


Complexity Analysis:

Time Complexity:
Building the Max Heap takes O(N) time.
Heapify operation takes O(log N) time.
The heapify operation is performed N times during sorting.
Therefore,

Time Complexity = O(N) + O(N log N)
                = O(N log N)
Best Case    = O(N log N)
Average Case = O(N log N)
Worst Case   = O(N log N)
